Time zone files for src/test/test_timezone_port.lua (section 4), which runs
its child process with TZDIR set to one of these directories.

They are zic output of the tz database (https://www.iana.org/time-zones,
public domain):

  slim/  zic -b slim: transitions up to the last rule change, later years
         from the POSIX rule in the file's footer
           America/New_York, Europe/Berlin
           EST5EDT      (a link to America/New_York in the tz database)
           posixrules   (America/New_York)
  fat/   zic -b fat: transitions written out up to 2037
           America/New_York, Europe/Berlin
           posixrules   (America/New_York)
         There is no EST5EDT here on purpose: the name is then read as a
         POSIX TZ string that takes the transitions of posixrules, as on a
         system that does not install the legacy zone names.

The expected values in the test come from Perl with the same TZDIR, so the
files must not be replaced by those of another tz release without
regenerating them.
